#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124193 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124579 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea4038bf-34f0-58cc-a7b6-6a4c1890570f" :knowledge-point/title "The Limit at Infinity for an Unbounded Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a5050a89-0b53-5499-8a78-9d5d7c5a78c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-11" :question/problem "The figure below shows the graph of $f(x).$ Find  $\\lim_\\limits{x \\rightarrow \\infty} f(x)$ and $\\lim_\\limits{x \\rightarrow -\\infty} f(x).$ \n\n![](images/c7/c7ee917a93ed51c189979516b9ab0d3232c183921ee277f522f617518ce03fdf.png)" :question/worked-solution "On the left side of the graph, we see that as the values of $x$ decrease and approach $-\\infty$, the graph of the function moves closer and closer to the horizontal asymptote $y=2.$ \n\nConsequently, $f(x)$ approaches the value $2$ as $x$ approaches $-\\infty,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -\\infty } f(x) = 2.\n$$\n\nOn the right side of the graph, as the values of $x$ increase and approach $\\infty,$ the graph of the function grows without bound to $\\infty$ as well. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\to \\infty } f(x) = \\infty.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124271 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124467 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cfbdc8f-6c4f-5411-b6f5-b7f0f046ac4f" :knowledge-point/title "The Limit at Infinity for a Bounded Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f0e213c5-8a7a-51a3-995f-394270a22bd2" :question/math-academy-id "e-3559" :question/problem "The figure below shows the graph of $f(x).$ Find the limit $\\lim_\\limits{x \\rightarrow \\infty} f(x).$ \n\n![](images/49/4982eb6e9020e5f6235049fd36a030a69d7b74a0e3ea60323ac8887f4c9bca79.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we see that as $x$ increases to $\\infty,$ the graph of the function moves closer to the horizontal asymptote $y=4.$\n\nTherefore, as $x$ approaches $\\infty,$ the function $f(x)$ approaches $4,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\infty } f(x) = 4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124579 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea4038bf-34f0-58cc-a7b6-6a4c1890570f" :knowledge-point/title "The Limit at Infinity for an Unbounded Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b42c29-5b27-5782-9407-a827fe74eada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=-2$ and ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545299} {:answer/id #uuid "432e6bf4-e493-5434-ae9a-e0016232e17c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=-2$ and ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=-\\infty $" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545325} {:answer/id #uuid "4deb45f9-98ed-520e-8fe2-1fe96ff3f473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=-2$ and ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=\\infty $" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545346} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2fc4cf-c91f-5e2b-ba44-7663cb5c839f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=0$ and ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=\\infty $" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545573} {:answer/id #uuid "dae4ec75-3a91-5668-b380-0a4af9b966a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=-\\infty $" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4deb45f9-98ed-520e-8fe2-1fe96ff3f473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=-2$ and ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=\\infty $" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545346} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea243ce2-45fd-5cec-817c-777d580842aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref